WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
("Cat &amp; Mouse Fight" by Swag House Mafia)

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.730
- [Narrator] Birches, birches, birches.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.220
Even more birches.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.100
Yes, thousands of birches everywhere.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.173
What is it about Umeå and
its passion for birch trees?

00:00:21.795 --> 00:00:24.962
- (speaks in Swedish)

00:00:31.526 --> 00:00:32.770
- [Narrator] And the residents of Umeå,

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.020
they use the birch for
just about everything.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.810
They use them for art,
they are painted on art,

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.160
they become furniture, decorate houses,

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.870
they color fabrics,
make medicine of birch,

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:46.263
glue and soaps, they make
tea and mixed drinks.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.040
Wait, what?

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:49.893
Is that right?

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:51.943
Drink birch?

00:00:52.993 --> 00:00:56.160
- (speaks in Swedish)

00:01:04.746 --> 00:01:07.913
- (speaks in Swedish)

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:14.750
- [Narrator] Even in the winter,

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.520
when the birches are bare and ugly,

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.400
they brighten up the town

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.850
but then, you have to go
indoors to peak at them.

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:30.320
But why is everyone in
Umeå so crazy for birches?

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.030
Given that it's winter most of year,

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:35.296
wouldn't pines have been
a more natural choice?

00:01:35.296 --> 00:01:38.463
- (speaks in Swedish)

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:45.740
- [Narrator] Okay, time for
a trip back into history.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:48.823
Let's rewind to Umeå in 1888.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.340
Back then, the whole town was,

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.420
more or less, built of wood.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.643
On June 25th, a fire broke
out in the city's brewery.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.570
Gale force winds caused the fire to spread

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:03.653
and grow to a disastrous size.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.670
The whole town burnt down.

00:02:07.646 --> 00:02:10.813
- (speaks in Swedish)

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.680
- [Narrator] That sounds pretty brilliant,

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:23.940
does it actually work?

00:02:25.794 --> 00:02:28.961
- (speaks in Swedish)

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:41.859
- [Narrator] Not everyone
is impressed by these trees.

00:02:41.859 --> 00:02:42.692
(sneeze)

00:02:42.692 --> 00:02:45.850
Lots of residents here
suffer from pollen allergies,

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:48.780
some so strong that they
can't bare to go outside

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.540
for parts of the year.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:54.150
So, how do locals coexist
with their city's symbol?

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.335
Is there a solution to this problem?

00:02:56.335 --> 00:02:59.502
- (speaks in Swedish)

00:03:11.162 --> 00:03:12.680
- [Narrator] Do you dare trust the tea?

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:15.293
Seems like it's worth a
visit to find out yourself.

